A||||8||Pretender||The Perfect heads??
Z||000000||Pretender||06-08-99||03:30 AM||||what would be the perfect head combo?., which rockers/valves/springs., and how would they be ported and polished to produce the highest hp gain.????should they be sent to a prof. shop?., if so does anyone reccomend a good performance shop that does work like this.., i plan on using a 50 shot of funny gas when i get them done., so i guess strength is also in big demand....thanks for your input.<br>
Z||000001||PaUL||06-08-99||06:23 PM||||The one unusual thing I noticed about the 2.8 heads are the fin-like obstructions in the intake ports. Ive read that if you port your heads, you should leave these fins alone. GM engineers designed these to increase intake velocity at low rpms. 
Z||000002||Eric||06-08-99||06:54 PM||||Yes, leave the fins alone.  
Z||000003||LEE498||06-08-99||10:13 PM||||I would recommend you send them off to a professional head porter, with a flow bench, and flow charts that way you can see the before and after cfm numbers. A good street- strip port job should cost about $500-$600, and should give you about 25-40hp depending on the cam you choose.  
Z||000004||Pretender||06-09-99||01:35 AM||||ok., i do plan on sending them out. is anyone running aftermarket roller rockers/valves or springs?., i think crane makes some for certin applications(unsure about mine)..if so were they worth the extra money?..
Z||000005||PaUL||06-09-99||02:21 AM||||Crane makes full roller rocker arms and lifters for the 2.8 but the rockers cost about $300 for 12. Competition Cams makes a roller tip set for about half as much, which is what I have on my car right now. Both come in 1.5 and 1.6 ratios.
Z||000006||Harry||06-12-99||03:50 PM||||I saw an artical once where a cam manufactor rolled an engine using an electric motor to turn it over. The temps on stock rockers ran about 250 deg F. where the same test using rollers (true rollers) the temps ran about 125 F. As in any good engineering practice loss of heat will equate to loss of friction which in turn give back horse power/performance and economy.<br>Roller food for thought.
Z||000007||Eric||06-12-99||05:32 PM||||Rollers can and do break.  The horsepower you would gain from installing a set would be at the top of the powerband.  They don't provide low end torque or horsepower.  I am going to retain the stock 1.5 rockers for my rebuild and save a $130 or so for a more useful project.
Z||000008||Pretender||06-12-99||10:55 PM||||thanks for all your info on this guys., but alas i have been BEATEN 2 TIMES TO MANY by ugly G'd up imports., i'm putting this 88gt back under the car-cover and taking off the insurance.......:o(
